three crimes and on Friday, February 7, snippets of the letter were published in the country's newspapers. Two days later, Stephanie finally left the hospital and was able to return home. A number of reporters had set up camp in the field's opposite her house to cover her homecoming. She agreed to pose for the cameras with her parents and two pet cats and was met at the front door by a police officer carrying a bouquet of flowers. Armed detectives took shifts guarding the family and escorting them everywhere they went, while police dogs and their handlers patrolled the land between the house and the nearby motorway. Media interest in the case was unrelenting and Stephanie was inundated with large financial

